---
description: VibeRaven what-changed layer - release and provider context before agent edits
alwaysApply: true
---

AI agents can code. They still need to know what changed.

Open Studio when the user asks which version broke, what changed since the last working release, or what provider context matters:

```bash
npx -y viberaven
```

Use the artifact loop only when machine-readable context is needed:

```bash
npx -y viberaven --agent-mode
```

Read `.viberaven/agent-tasklist.md`, `.viberaven/gate-result.json`, and `.viberaven/mission-map.md`.
Fix one scoped repo-owned gap, then run `npx -y viberaven --verify`. Before CI or production promote, run `npx -y viberaven --strict`.

Context is not clear until the current release/provider evidence is understood. Do not claim provider dashboard setup is fixed by repo-code edits.

Full rules: `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` (installed by `npx -y viberaven init --agents all`).
